 34CL    9BE(37CA,34CLG)               2010DO03                  ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL c  {+37}Ca|)3p+{+34}Cl on {+9}Be target.                                  
 34CL c  2010Do03: a 420-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca primary beam was provided from the 
 34CL2c  heavy ion synchrotron SIS at GSI and impinged on a 4-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be  
 34CL3c  target. {+37}Ca was selected by FRS and was incident on a 700-mg/cm{+2}
 34CL4c  secondary {+9}Be target at 195.7 MeV/u. {+34}Cl was produced via a     
 34CL5c  secondary three proton removal reaction. |g rays were detected using   
 34CL6c  the RISING setup consisting of 15 Cluster HPGe detectors, 8 MINIBALL   
 34CL7c  HPGe detectors, and 8 Hector BaF{-2} detectors. Fragments were detected
 34CL8c  using the calorimeter telescope CATE consisting of position sensitive  
 34CL9c  Si |DE detectors and CsI(Tl) E{-res} detectors. Measured E|g, I|g.     
 34CLAc  Deduced lifetime using Doppler Shift Attenuation lineshape analysis    
 34CLBc  (2010Do03) and peak-shift analysis (2007DoZV).                         
